---
description: Domain rules for generating tests from OpenAPI specs (providers, rules, models, codegen)
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

You are extending and maintaining the OpenAPI-driven test generation flow.

- Architecture overview
  - `TestGenerationEngine` orchestrates: parse OpenAPI → `TestGenerationProcessor.generateReport` → `ArtifactGenerator.generateTests`.
  - `TestGeneratorConfigurer` wires providers and rules using explicit manual wiring via `ManualRuleRegistry` and `BuiltInRules`.
  - Providers derive negative cases from a baseline valid case built by `ValidCaseBuilder`.
  - `ProviderOrchestrator` executes providers in fixed order; `OutcomeAggregator` combines results.

- ValidCaseBuilder
  - Constructs baseline valid `TestCase` from operation parameters, body, and security.
  - Uses `SecurityValueProvider` with `validSecurityValues` from `TestGenerationSettings`.
  - Uses `SchemaExampleValueGenerator` to derive values from schema examples or defaults.
  - Handles required parameters and first supported media type (JSON preferred).

- TestGenerationContext
  - Interface providing shared state: `openAPI`, `operation`, `validCase`, helpers (`basicTestData`, `securityValueProvider`, `schemaExampleValueGenerator`, `schemaMerger`).
  - Tracks depth via `maxDepth` and schema explosion via `combinationBudget`.
  - `DefaultTestGenerationContext` is the standard implementation.
  - Pass context to providers; avoid global state.

- Providers
  - Each provider implements `TestCaseProvider<T>` and must be pure (no mutations of inputs).
  - For parameters and request bodies: dereference `$ref` via helpers before applying rules.
  - Set `expectedStatusCode = 400` for generated negative cases unless a different behavior is specified.
  - Derive names using concise, user-facing phrasing (see existing tests for style).
  - Use `TestGenerationContext` to pass both the valid baseline and OpenAPI context; avoid global state.
  - Favor composition of smaller providers per concern (missing required vs schema violation) to keep behavior focused and testable.
  - Providers return `Outcome<List<TestCase>>`; use `runProviderSafely` to wrap execution.

- Rules
  - `SchemaValidationRule` and `AuthValidationRule` implementations must:
    - Return `Sequence<RuleValue>` without side effects.
    - Be defensive against null schemas and unsupported types; return empty sequence when not applicable.
    - Use helpers from `SchemaTypeHelpers` and `BasicTestDataProvider` where appropriate.
  - Keep composed rules (`ArrayItemSchemaValidationRule`, `ObjectItemSchemaValidationRule`) injectable; do not hardcode dependencies.
  - Keep rule evaluation pure and order-stable; `BuiltInRules` sorts by rule name, and `ManualRuleRegistry` re-sorts by class name.

- Valid case building
  - `ValidCaseBuilder` must include only supported media types and required params.
  - Enforce security scheme constraints; fail fast with clear messages for unsupported security.
  - Use `SecurityValueProvider` with `validSecurityValues` from `TestGenerationSettings`.
  - Respect `overrideBasicTestData` via `BasicTestDataProvider`.

- Code generation
  - `ArtifactGenerator` implementations emit deterministic code; prefer Mustache over string concatenation.
  - Keep `TemplateArtifactGenerator` focused on I/O and generation; avoid parsing responsibilities.
  - For `TestSuiteWriter`, honor options from `TestSuiteWriterOptions` including `writeMode`, `format`, and `protectedTestCaseFields`.
  - For any new generator, separate option validation from generation and reuse common helpers for naming/indentation.

- Budget controls
  - `maxSchemaDepth`: Limits recursion in nested schemas (default 10).
  - `maxSchemaCombinations`: Limits allOf/anyOf/oneOf explosion (default 100).
  - `maxTestCasesPerOperation`: Caps test cases per operation (default 500).
  - `CombinationBudget` throws `BudgetExceededException` when limits exceeded.
  - `TestCaseBudgetValidator` enforces per-operation limits and trims excess deterministically.
  - Budget violations produce `GenerationError` with meaningful context.

- Performance and determinism
  - Preserve order: `BuiltInRules` sorts by rule name, `ManualRuleRegistry` re-sorts by class name, and `BuiltInGenerators` sorts by generator id.
  - No reflection is used for rule/generator discovery; wiring is explicit and compile-time safe.
  - When filtering ignored test cases, apply path → method → name filtering in a stable order.

- Error handling and reporting
  - The system uses `Outcome<T>` as a result type with `Success`, `PartialSuccess`, or `Failure`.
  - Providers return `Outcome<List<TestCase>>`; `runProviderSafely` converts exceptions to `Outcome.Failure`.
  - `GenerationReport` aggregates all test suites and errors from the generation process.
  - `ErrorHandlingConfig` controls error behavior:
    - `ErrorMode.FAIL_FAST`: stop on first error
    - `ErrorMode.COLLECT_ALL`: collect all errors up to `maxErrors` limit
  - `BudgetExceededException` is thrown when schema complexity limits are exceeded (combinations, test cases per operation) and is converted at provider boundaries.
  - Use `mergeTestCaseOutcomes(...)` helper to combine multiple `Outcome` results.
  - Always include meaningful context in errors (`ErrorContext` with operation, path, rule name).

- Testing
  - Add tests alongside changes; ensure negative and positive cases are covered for new rules/providers.

